Solution: Note that the graphs of $y=g(x)$ and $y=h(x)$ are the reflections of the graph of $y=f(x)$ across the $x$-axis and the $y$-axis, respectively. Thus, the original graph intersects these two graphs at its $x$-intercepts and $y$-intercepts, respectively. This is shown in the following picture: [asy]
size(150);
