Solution: Let $s$ be the side length of the square. Also let $D$ be the vertex of the square on side $AC$, and let $E$ be the vertex of the square on side $AB$. Let $F$ and $G$ be the feet of the altitudes from $D$ and $A$ to $BC$, respectively. Let $x$ be the length of $AD$.

